    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Client Intake\nNew client submits the form. The workflow validates it, rejects bad or duplicate entries, creates the client's records, sends a welcome email, and logs every outcome.\n**Data:** NocoDB (clients, documents, tasks, activity_log) | **Email:** Mailpit (test only)\n**Errors:** shared handler emails staff",
        "height": 272,
        "width": 800,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -16,
        -1280
      ],
      "id": "895b45e4-582d-4450-8d01-85c6f60b9d25",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Receive and clean\n**In:** form answers\n**Logic:** config values live in SetConfig (no hard-coding). The email is trimmed and lower-cased so \"A@x.com \" and \"a@x.com\" match.\n**Out:** email_clean for every later step\n**Note:** email is a Text field on purpose, so bad input reaches the server-side check",
        "height": 368,
        "width": 592,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -16,
        -656
      ],
      "id": "28936ae9-6255-4486-94a5-a1decfdddd33",
      "name": "Sticky Note1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n## 2. Validate email\n**Logic:** regex format check (not proof the address exists)\n**If invalid:** log \"invalid_email_rejected\", show a rejection page\n**Why log first:** the form's completion node ends the request, so anything to record must happen before it",
        "height": 384,
        "width": 592,
        "color": "#BD0000"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        656,
        -464
      ],
      "id": "fcd1871b-d84c-4d00-a542-4ec92b75d03d",
      "name": "Sticky Note2"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Duplicate check\n**Logic:** search clients by email. Always Output Data is ON so \"no match\" still reaches the IF.\n**If duplicate:** log it, email staff, show rejection\n**Gotcha:** NocoDB nests columns under `fields`, so the check reads $json.fields?.email\n**Execute Once ON** on the log and alert: one entry per attempt",
        "height": 416,
        "width": 1152
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        864,
        -1040
      ],
      "id": "629f7f87-c43a-4b3b-8df1-3b450652f235",
      "name": "Sticky Note3"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n## 4. Create records\n**Out:** 1 client (status awaiting_documents), 2 tasks, 4 documents (6 for \"large\" businesses)\n**How:** Code nodes output several items; the NocoDB node after each runs once per item.\n**Columns mapped by hand:** auto-map left the document rows empty",
        "height": 384,
        "width": 1312,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1344,
        -464
      ],
      "id": "11357f8f-53ec-4a08-82c8-d0f79261fac8",
      "name": "Sticky Note4"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5. Welcome and finish\n**Logic:** one email listing the required documents. Execute Once ON (one email, not one per document). Retry On Fail ON.\n**Out:** welcome email, log entry, success page\n**Limit:** template email. An AI-written version is a planned extension.",
        "height": 416,
        "width": 704,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2752,
        -640
      ],
      "id": "1a940db6-1afb-47fe-b8c7-da45ea2d2467",
      "name": "Sticky Note5"
    }
